e(4,'c',7,6,'Explain','Explain how two data mining techniques could be applied to provide a different view of the data displayed on this map.',C,['A3.4.3'],'B',8,'OldMSoffersmapfilters/heatmaps;not automatically the2027must-include mining techniques.','Explain how clustering andclassification could each support analysis of emergency-call records containing location,time andincident attributes.',pts((1,'Clustering groups records with similar features without requiring preassigned class labels.'),(1,'It can reveal geographically/time-related groups of incidents.'),(1,'Those groups may inform resource placement but require contextual interpretation.'),(1,'Classification learns relationships from labelled example incidents.'),(1,'It predicts a discrete category for a new record,e.g.incident priority.'),(1,'Predictions must be evaluated against known outcomes rather than treating a map filter as a learned classifier.')),reason='Retains analytical application reasoning;substitutes exact2027required clustering/classification for sourceMS visual-filter examples.')
e(4,'d',7,5,'Discuss','Discuss the ethics of using visual data analysis tools.',C+'Political parties may display maps differently.',['A4.4.1'],'B',8,'Selective presentation can mislead;transparency andpublicbenefits vsagenda manipulation.','Discuss ethical concerns when a city publishes an AI-generated crime-risk map that influences police deployment.',pts((1,'Biased historical reporting can produce unfair risk estimates.'),(1,'Feedback from deployment can reinforce unequal scrutiny of communities.'),(1,'Transparent labels,uncertainty anddata limitations help users interpret the map.'),(1,'Accountability andhuman review are needed when decisions affect people.'),(1,'Balanced conclusion weighs public-safety benefits against fairness/privacy risks in this context.')),reason='Retains selective-analysis/ethicaljudgment but explicitly ties it torequiredMLfairness,transparency andaccountability.')
